al moments in the video, repeatedly watching and recommending it. The content elicited reactions even from those who do not typically like Donald Trump.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T18:51:13.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108629581263786373"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108216880976773548"},{"post_id":"2108408416007754069"},{"post_id":"2108414235885683073"},{"post_id":"2108376771976675445"},{"post_id":"2108424468326732226"},{"post_id":"2108408416007754069"},{"post_id":"2108414235885683073"},{"post_id":"2108376771976675445"},{"post_id":"2108295008558235654"},{"post_id":"2108386338298908911"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Memes"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Purple-clad performers stack into flowing waves and towering skyscrapers, their synchronized moves leaving viewers questioning what's real.","id":"2108435158269382743","name":"AI-Generated Acrobats Build Jaw-Dropping Human Pyramids","summary":"Videos watermark-marked 'GRANDORA SHOW' or 'Dola AI' depict acrobats forming dynamic human pyramids that bend like waves, rise into skyscrapers, and mimic robotic arms across arena floors. Fact-checkers confirm these are AI-generated, with unnatural movements, inconsistent details, and disclaimers noting they're fictional creations not to be attempted. Even with clarifications, the clips draw huge engagement as people marvel at the teamwork illusion and debate the line between real feats and synthetic visuals.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T05:56:36.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108435158269382743"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108543413436264625"},{"post_id":"2108560286395617406"},{"post_id":"2108603417145016793"},{"post_id":"2108606158709903863"},{"post_id":"2108594346169946488"},{"post_id":"2108560554713301229"},{"post_id":"2108595421874618369"},{"post_id":"2108579711383134672"},{"post_id":"210